// ELF (System V ABI, 32/64-bit, either byte order); ids and names are public
// API. The reader validates the whole header, program header
// and section header layout before the script runs (Format.size() is -1
// otherwise), so the script re-reads those tables with the reader's rules:
// extended counts from section 0, p_filesz clamped to the end of the file.
//
// Every structure uses the file byte order. Several records are logical views
// of one stored value (st_bind, r_sym, vs_index, ...): the record keeps the raw
// bytes and displays the derived value in decimal. Byte arrays display as
